# counter harness. One force call is one RgpotCounter.calculate entry.
# v2 success is under the cap, at the force stop, and Hessian index 0.
# energy and Kabsch RMSD were not applied: the problem file has no energy_tol, rmsd_tol, or per-start reference.
# energy_min and energy_max are the final potential values on the recorded points.
# Default row. gtol and the iteration budget are the problem force norm and the force-call cap. The template sets no maxstep, so the Cartesian default per-atom cap of 0.2 applies. istep is 0.1. SR2 is Powell's symmetric Broyden update in the SR1 trust region: dogleg when the model is positive definite, otherwise the Cauchy point. The trust radius opens at 0.2 times the square root of the atom count, the Euclidean ball of one capped per-atom step. There is no line search. The same values are used for every start.
